WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.569
Morse: "Cleaning your fruits
and vegetables with bleach

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:03.803
is effective."

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:05.305
Madad: That is completely false.

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:05.338
We used to think that.

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:07.707
Morse: "All schools should reopen

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:11.177
because kids can't get COVID-19."

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:12.912
We used to think that.

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:15.115
But now we know it's not true.

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:16.883
Hi, I'm Stephen Morse,

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:19.185
professor of epidemiology.

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:20.787
My name is Dr. Syra Madad,

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:23.390
and I'm an infectious
disease epidemiologist

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:24.758
here in New York City.

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:28.294
Morse: In the past, we have
debunked a number of myths.

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:30.030
But new myths keep coming up,

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.465
and the same old ones keep coming back.

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:36.136
So let's get to work
debunking more myths today.

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:38.371
Madad: "Wearing a mask
doesn't do anything."

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.440
Morse: And there are
people who believe that.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.643
And one reason is that until recently,

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:45.979
we weren't really recommending masks

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:49.749
because we didn't know that
they actually do a lot of good.

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:52.018
There's a recent study from Hong Kong

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:53.753
that was published in Nature

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:56.423
that proves that even surgical masks

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:58.625
can prevent infected people

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:01.761
from passing on the infection to others.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:04.097
Madad: We have seen that in states

00:01:04.097 --> 00:01:05.899
that didn't have a mask mandate,

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:07.500
once they had that mask mandate,

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.202
over a period of time, you did see

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:10.703
the number of cases go down.

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:12.739
So it's important to
continue to wash your hands

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:15.008
and keep your distance
while also wearing a mask.

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:16.943
Morse: "Wearing a mask is dangerous

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:20.113
because you'll get carbon
dioxide poisoning."

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:22.916
But it takes a lot of
carbon dioxide to do it,

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:24.384
and all of that actually

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:26.853
goes through the mask quite readily.

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:29.422
So it doesn't build up in the mask.

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:33.159
And we know that even when
people are wearing masks,

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:36.062
their oxygen levels in the blood

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:39.466
are perfectly normal if they're not sick.

00:01:39.466 --> 00:01:42.235
So part of it is really
getting used to it,

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:45.605
the way we get used to wearing
a necktie, for example.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:47.340
Madad: Looking at those healthcare workers

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.008
that do wear it for an
extended period of time,

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:50.343
that's a great model to show you

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:54.280
that it does not cause carbon
dioxide poisoning or toxicity.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.683
Morse: "All schools should reopen

00:01:56.683 --> 00:02:00.186
because kids can't get COVID-19."

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:02.589
Once the schools reopen,

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:04.124
we're gonna see a situation

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:06.693
where there are a lot of kids together

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:11.698
and the possibility of
transmission becomes much greater.

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:13.967
Madad: And on top of that,
it's not also just the kids,

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:15.802
it's also the teachers and the adults

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:16.903
that are in these schools

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:18.638
that are also at risk.

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:20.340
And so we wanna protect everybody.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.808
There are countries in Asia

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:24.277
that have reopened schools successfully

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:26.012
and have been able to remain open.

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:29.015
They started off with
having low number of cases,

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:31.184
and they also had
contingency plans in place

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:33.186
where you have smaller classroom sizes,

00:02:33.186 --> 00:02:35.889
children sitting further
apart, wearing masks.

00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:37.557
You also have countries that have shown

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:39.759
that they opened schools too early,

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:41.761
and then they had to
close down multiple times.

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:43.830
And so we wanna make
sure we're in a position

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:44.998
that we have the upper hand

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:46.499
when it comes to this virus.

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.801
"Asymptomatic people aren't contagious."

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:51.704
Morse: Asymptomatic
people, people who feel

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:53.640
and look perfectly well,

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:55.909
are contagious to others.

00:02:55.909 --> 00:02:57.744
And we worry about them

00:02:57.744 --> 00:03:00.480
because they may not know
what they're spreading.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.448
Madad: In fact, during the early days,

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:04.350
that is when you are most infectious.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.986
Morse: The reality is we have to assume

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:09.489
that anyone who could have it,

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:11.424
indeed could have it,

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:13.693
and they could pass it on to others.

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:16.462
This is why we're making recommendations

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:18.998
that everybody should wear a mask,

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:20.700
even if they're feeling well,

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:24.637
because we don't know and
they themselves may not know

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:26.439
that they could be infected

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:28.341
and able to infect others.

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:31.578
Madad: "Young, healthy people
won't die from COVID-19."

00:03:31.578 --> 00:03:34.847
We have seen cases where
you have individuals

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:36.583
that have no medical condition

00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:39.485
still unfortunately die from COVID-19.

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:42.488
Morse: It may be a very small proportion,

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:45.959
but when you have a very large
number of infected people,

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:48.861
those numbers add up very quickly.

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:50.697
Madad: We are seeing,
based on certain data

00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:53.199
that is coming out, is that
even with young people,

00:03:53.199 --> 00:03:55.835
if they don't have a
severe case of COVID-19,

00:03:55.835 --> 00:03:58.204
they are at increased risk, for example,

00:03:58.204 --> 00:04:00.173
of strokes and other types of ailments.

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:01.841
And so looking at the
death rate in the young

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:03.910
is a false sense of security.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:07.413
Morse: "You cannot get COVID-19 twice."

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:08.314
Madad: We still don't know

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:09.816
what long-term immunity looks like,

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:11.985
and so in the immediate future,

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:13.886
can you get reinfected with COVID-19

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:14.988
in a short period of time?

00:04:14.988 --> 00:04:16.789
The likelihood is no.

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:19.325
Individuals that have
been tested positive again

00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:22.562
for COVID-19 likely
just have residual virus

00:04:22.562 --> 00:04:24.430
in their body or in their bodily fluids.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.566
But in terms of long term,

00:04:26.566 --> 00:04:30.670
can you get COVID-19 a year
after or two years after?

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.739
That is something that
we still don't know yet,

00:04:32.739 --> 00:04:34.841
and it's one of those
things that time will tell.

00:04:34.841 --> 00:04:38.044
Morse: If you get it
again, will it be less bad,

00:04:38.044 --> 00:04:40.480
will it be worse, will it be the same?

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:41.547
We don't know.

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:43.850
Madad: "You won't get the
virus if you hold your breath

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:45.752
when someone sneezes or coughs."

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:47.387
But what we know about
these virus particles

00:04:47.387 --> 00:04:49.622
is that they can still
land on your mucus membrane

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:50.990
even if you're not breathing.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:53.192
So, for example, if you're
touching a high-touch surface

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:54.894
and then you're touching
your mucus membrane,

00:04:54.894 --> 00:04:57.163
you obviously are able
to transmit the virus

00:04:57.163 --> 00:04:59.732
through that indirect means, if you will.

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:01.534
Morse: So, we have alternatives.

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:05.338
We have masks, we have good hand hygiene,

00:05:05.338 --> 00:05:07.140
and social distancing

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:11.644
to make sure that you won't
be in the line of fire

00:05:11.644 --> 00:05:14.080
when somebody coughs or sneezes.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.816
That's a lot safer than
holding your breath.

00:05:16.816 --> 00:05:19.118
Madad: "Consuming disinfectants
will kill the virus."

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:22.555
Bleach and other types of disinfectants

00:05:22.555 --> 00:05:25.725
are not to be used for ingesting

00:05:25.725 --> 00:05:28.828
or injecting or to put on skin.

00:05:28.828 --> 00:05:30.530
These are corrosive chemicals.

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:32.799
They can actually cause
death and disability.

00:05:32.799 --> 00:05:36.436
Morse: Use it on your floors.
Use it on your countertops.

00:05:36.436 --> 00:05:38.638
That's where it really does the work,

00:05:38.638 --> 00:05:40.740
and that's what really helps.

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:42.241
"Cleaning your fruits and vegetables

00:05:42.241 --> 00:05:44.344
with bleach is effective."

00:05:44.344 --> 00:05:45.845
Madad: That is completely false.

00:05:45.845 --> 00:05:47.180
If you're going to be putting chemicals

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:49.649
on fruit and vegetables that
you are then going to ingest,

00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:51.284
you're putting yourself
more in harm's way.

00:05:51.284 --> 00:05:52.819
So, washing your fruit and vegetables

00:05:52.819 --> 00:05:54.854
is very similar to how you
were washing your fruit

00:05:54.854 --> 00:05:56.689
and vegetables before COVID-19 existed.

00:05:56.689 --> 00:05:59.225
Washing it under water and making sure

00:05:59.225 --> 00:06:00.927
that you're cleaning
any fruit and vegetable.

00:06:00.927 --> 00:06:03.029
These are just basic good practices.

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:04.464
'Cause it's not just COVID-19

00:06:04.464 --> 00:06:05.832
that obviously you wanna make sure

00:06:05.832 --> 00:06:07.467
that you are preventing,

00:06:07.467 --> 00:06:09.235
but it's also all the other microbes

00:06:09.235 --> 00:06:10.937
that can cause illnesses.

00:06:10.937 --> 00:06:13.206
"Warm weather will stop the coronavirus."

00:06:13.206 --> 00:06:15.475
Morse: Well, here we
are at the end of July,

00:06:15.475 --> 00:06:17.910
and if anyone still believes that myth,

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:19.879
I think we have plenty of proof.

00:06:19.879 --> 00:06:22.248
Madad: There's an epidemiological
potential significance

00:06:22.248 --> 00:06:25.084
to warmer weather because
people are going outside,

00:06:25.084 --> 00:06:27.453
but in terms of the weather itself

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:29.322
and the effect on the virus,

00:06:29.322 --> 00:06:31.524
it has not shown to have impact.

00:06:31.524 --> 00:06:34.460
Morse: So, until we find
something like a vaccine

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:36.729
that's effective or something else

00:06:36.729 --> 00:06:38.364
that's going to stop it,

00:06:38.364 --> 00:06:41.634
this virus, given the
opportunity to infect,

00:06:41.634 --> 00:06:43.136
will continue to infect.

00:06:43.136 --> 00:06:47.740
"99% of cases aren't dangerous."

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:50.910
Yes, it is true that probably

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:53.212
only about 1%

00:06:53.212 --> 00:06:56.315
of those people who get infected

00:06:56.315 --> 00:07:00.186
and get sick are going to die,

00:07:00.186 --> 00:07:03.756
but many of the others will get very sick,

00:07:03.756 --> 00:07:06.959
and some of the others will get so sick

00:07:06.959 --> 00:07:09.128
that they may be affected for life.

00:07:09.128 --> 00:07:12.498
Madad: Our indicator should
not be the death rate,

00:07:12.498 --> 00:07:14.300
because you can have individuals

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:17.837
that may have survived
the infection of COVID-19

00:07:17.837 --> 00:07:20.306
but then go on to suffer a stroke

00:07:20.306 --> 00:07:23.309
because of the long-term
effects of COVID-19.

00:07:23.309 --> 00:07:27.847
Morse: So a lot of these
cases really are dangerous.

00:07:27.847 --> 00:07:29.048
Madad: "The United States has one

00:07:29.048 --> 00:07:30.950
of the lowest mortality rates."

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:32.985
Taking the mortality at its face value

00:07:32.985 --> 00:07:34.086
is a huge disservice

00:07:34.086 --> 00:07:36.055
because it's not painting the full picture

00:07:36.055 --> 00:07:38.157
in terms of the whole effect

00:07:38.157 --> 00:07:41.060
that COVID-19 has on an individual.

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:43.596
Morse: Unfortunately, when you think about

00:07:43.596 --> 00:07:47.467
the entire population on mortality rate,

00:07:47.467 --> 00:07:50.336
it's actually unbelievably high.

00:07:50.336 --> 00:07:52.939
We don't really want to measure this

00:07:52.939 --> 00:07:54.607
by the number of people

00:07:54.607 --> 00:07:57.143
who get saved at the last minute.

00:07:57.143 --> 00:08:02.081
What we wanna aim for is
really a low infection rate,

00:08:02.081 --> 00:08:04.817
because the infection is gonna be there.

00:08:04.817 --> 00:08:07.720
Mortality rate proves
you're just getting better

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:10.823
at treating the severe cases.

00:08:10.823 --> 00:08:13.459
Madad: "5G technology
is spreading COVID-19."

00:08:13.459 --> 00:08:16.696
COVID-19 is spread by respiratory droplets

00:08:16.696 --> 00:08:20.032
when somebody coughs, sneezes, or talks.

00:08:20.032 --> 00:08:23.736
5G towers and technology
do not have an influence

00:08:23.736 --> 00:08:26.806
on your ability to get
infected with COVID-19.

00:08:26.806 --> 00:08:30.743
Morse: The reality is the
two are totally unrelated.

00:08:30.743 --> 00:08:33.179
You can spread computer viruses

00:08:33.179 --> 00:08:35.748
through technology on the internet,

00:08:35.748 --> 00:08:39.886
but real viruses requires human contact.

00:08:39.886 --> 00:08:43.823
"The media is blowing the
pandemic out of proportion."

00:08:43.823 --> 00:08:45.892
I really wish this were true.

00:08:45.892 --> 00:08:47.260
And I think it depends a lot

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:49.529
on which media you're listening to.

00:08:49.529 --> 00:08:52.365
By talking about conspiracy theories

00:08:52.365 --> 00:08:55.668
and "no big deal," to
say that it's all a hoax,

00:08:55.668 --> 00:08:57.904
these things help the virus.

00:08:57.904 --> 00:08:59.539
The virus doesn't care.

00:08:59.539 --> 00:09:03.142
The reality is it's here, it's real,

00:09:03.142 --> 00:09:06.345
it will infect given the opportunity.

00:09:06.345 --> 00:09:08.347
Madad: It is science, and it is evidence,

00:09:08.347 --> 00:09:10.850
and it is public health
that will save lives.

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:14.954
It's not politicians, it's
not conspiracy theories,

00:09:14.954 --> 00:09:16.422
it's not misinformation.

00:09:16.422 --> 00:09:18.391
And as we continue to learn together,

00:09:18.391 --> 00:09:20.059
the public-health guidance will change,

00:09:20.059 --> 00:09:23.462
because we wanna go with
what we know to be effective

00:09:23.462 --> 00:09:25.731
in terms of keeping everybody safe.

00:09:25.731 --> 00:09:29.101
Morse: Stay safe, stay well, and...

00:09:29.101 --> 00:09:30.303
Madad: Stay tuned and stay informed,

00:09:30.303 --> 00:09:31.971
and that's very important.

